<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia's Sept 1-25 palm oil exports 528,150T-SGS.</title>
<headline>Malaysia's Sept 1-25 palm oil exports 528,150T-SGS.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cargo surveyor, Societe Generale de Surveillance (SGS) Malaysia Sdn Bhd said on Wednesday said it estimated Malaysia's palm oil exports for September 1-25 at 528,150 tonnes compared with 537,175 in Aug 1-25.</p>
<p>It said the exports comprised 108,205 tonnes of RBD palm oil, 263,268 tonnes of RBD palm olein and 76,890 tonnes of RBD palm stearin. The other products accounted for 79,787 tonnes.  </p>
<p>India was the top buyer during the period, taking 129,916 tonnes, followed by China which bought at 67,565 tonnes, Pakistan 56,130 tonnes and Egypt 37,250 tonnes.</p>
<p>Countries in the European Union bought 31,864 tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-230-8911)</p>
